Project 5: Ask Your Notes: AI Document Q&A (Capstone)

What it is. An app where a user uploads PDFs, for example their semester notes or a company policy
document, and asks questions in plain language. The app finds the most relevant parts of the documents
and uses a large language model to answer, showing which page each answer came from.
Why it impresses. This is the kind of AI feature companies are actually building in 2026. It proves you
understand more than prompting: chunking text, embeddings, vector search, retrieval, cost and failure
cases. Combined with your backend projects, it makes your profile stand out strongly.

Tech stack

Tech                            stack
Backend                         FastAPI
PDF reading                     pypdf
Embeddings                      An open source model through the sentence_transformers library, or an embeddings
                                API
Vector store                    ChromaDB or FAISS while learning, pgvector inside PostgreSQL later
LLM                             An LLM API with a free developer tier, for example Google's Gemini API or Groq.
                                Check current free limits before you start.
Interface                       Streamlit at first
Database                        PostgreSQL for users, documents and chat history

Must have features
• Upload one or more PDFs, extract text, split it into chunks with page numbers.
• Create embeddings for each chunk and store them in the vector database.
• For each question, retrieve the top matching chunks and send them with the question to the LLM.
• Show the answer with sources (document name and page number).
• If the answer is not in the documents, the app must clearly say so instead of making something up.
• Save chat history per user.
Extra features once the basics work
• A small evaluation set: twenty questions with known answers, and a score for how many your app
gets right.
• Track response time and approximate cost per question.
• Streaming responses so the answer appears word by word.
• Support for Word files and web pages.
